fact WorkItem(id: "WI-1005", description: some(value: "One AMBIGUITY, reported TWICE — an occurrence remapped at two scopes, and WI-745's dedup cannot see it.\n\nFOUND WHILE DRIVING WI-994, which made the shape reachable and PINNED the\ndouble rather than fixing it (wi994_variant_exposure_test::\none_variant_name_exposed_by_two_namespaces_is_ambiguous expects 5 errors, of\nwhich 2 are the same finding).\n\nMEASURED. One occurrence at 6:7, two errors:\n  6:7: ambiguous symbol 'guarded' in scope 'p':   candidates [...]\n  6:7: ambiguous symbol 'guarded' in scope 'amb': candidates [...]\n'p' is the operation, 'amb' the enclosing namespace — the same written name\nremapped once per scope. Only the AMBIGUITY rows double; the field-label and\ntype-mismatch rows for the same occurrence appear once, so this is not a\ngeneral 2x on name remapping and the cause is specific to the ambiguity path.\n\nWHY THE EXISTING DEDUP MISSES IT. LoadError::dedup_key is deliberately\nINJECTIVE — the full rendering, span included — and its doc says so on purpose:\ntwo references to one bad name in same-short-named but DISTINCT scopes must\nboth survive, since a short scope name is not a unique identity\n(no-short-name-comparison). Here the two renderings differ ONLY in the scope\nname, so nothing collapses them. WI-745 met the same class of duplicate (a head\nfunctor resolved for owner-tracking AND for the term build) and eliminated it\nAT THE PRODUCER for exactly this reason; this is a second producer pair doing\nthe same. WI-745's own CLI test asserts the property this violates —\nrun_cmd_test.rs asserts the ambiguous-symbol message appears exactly once.\n\nEASY TO MISS, which is why it went unnoticed: name the namespace and the\noperation alike and the two renderings COINCIDE and dedup. The probe WI-994 was\nwritten from did exactly that (namespace wi994.p, operation p) and reported\n4 errors; the test fixture renamed the namespace and reported 5.\n\nWORK: find the two producers (there are 5 push_ambiguous_symbol call sites in\nkb/load.rs, one shared spelling) and establish which two both remap the SAME\noccurrence at different current_scope values — then eliminate one, as WI-745\ndid, rather than widening dedup_key. Widening it is refused for the reason its\ndoc already gives.\n\nACCEPTANCE: the wi994 fixture reports the ambiguity ONCE (the pinned list drops\nto 4, and that edit is the test the fix must come with); the WI-745 CLI\ncount-is-1 assertion still holds; a CONTROL showing two genuinely distinct\nreferences to one bad name in two scopes still report twice. cargo-test green\nvia rustland/scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
